  "comments": "In 1911, the Dominion Parks Division, now known as Parks Canada, was born with a mandate to conserve Canada's splendid natural landscapes for the well-being of Canadians.<br /><br />\nBy creating the world's first national park system, Canada was inscribing the conservation of natural sites in our values, and encouraging other countries to protect their own wilderness areas.<br /><br />\nFor a century, Parks Canada has been the dedicated guardian and faithful protector of Canada's immense and magnificent natural treasures, preserving them not only for the enjoyment of Canadians, but for people around the world and for generations to come.",
